.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-DELETE-ACCOUNT 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-delete-account \- delete a Euclid account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam delete-account
.BR \-\-account\-id | \-a
.I ACCOUNTID
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes the account identified by \fIACCOUNTID\fR via the eam service's
.I delete-account
action. The caller must be authenticated as a global administrator (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1)).
.PP
The account must first have every one of its namespaces deleted (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-namespace (1))
and every user grant referencing it revoked (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-revoke-namespace-access (1)) -
the server rejects the request with \fIHTTP 409\fR otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-account\-id " " \fIACCOUNTID\fR
Account ID of the account to delete. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The account was deleted.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, the caller is
not an authenticated global administrator, no account with that ID
exists, or the account still has namespaces or user grants (\fIHTTP
409\fR). If the failure was an expired or invalid session (\fIHTTP
401\fR), the stored credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam delete-account \e
    --account-id 123456789012
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-account (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-list-accounts (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-namespace (1)
